In article <1993May10.025413.24415@mnemosyne.cs.du.edu>, ssprunk@nyx.cs.du.edu (Stephen Sprunk) writes:
> 
> I was wondering if my sister can, while she is on vacation, have all her
> mail forwarded to my account where she is for the summer.  I know this is
> possible with UNIX's .forward file, but I know next to nothing of VMS.  

    This should just be a matter of either logging into her account and
    doing a 

    MAIL>  SET FORWARD forwarding_address

    or getting her system manager or suitably privileged person (SYSNAM is
    required) to do a 

    MAIL>  SET FORWARD/USER=her_username forwarding_address

    If her system is running PMDF, I think the command is:

    $ PMDF FORWARD forwarding_address

    Actual format of "forwarding_address" varies depending on your
    transport and mailer (VMSMail, ALL-IN-FUN), but will usually look
    something like:

    MX%"user@host.dom"  (or user@host.dom for PMDF)

    maybe with extra quotes.  See the documentation for your mailer or ask
    her system manager.

> [...]Also, is it possible to do a TALK on a
> Internet UNIX machine to a Bitnet VAX/VMS machine?

    Probably, but I don't have the slightest idea how.  Someone will.... 
    :-)


    WordMan
